    <h2>The Bottom Line</h2>
    <p>The real numbers in 2026 tell a nuanced story. Buying is not always better than renting, and renting is not always better than buying. The answer depends on your city, your time horizon, the size of your deposit, what you would do with the money if you didn't buy, and whether you have the discipline to invest the savings that renting can generate.</p>
    <p>What the numbers do confirm is this: the true annual cost of homeownership is substantially higher than the monthly repayment figure suggests, and the case for buying is strongest for people who plan to stay put for the long term in markets with strong demand fundamentals and reasonable price-to-rent ratios.</p>
    <p>Before making the biggest financial decision of your life, run the numbers for your specific situation.</p>

